          "worked": "The original domain is $x\\ne0$. Let $u=\\ln(x^2)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-6u+8&=0\\\\(u-2)(u-4)&=0\\\\u&=2\\text{ or }4\\\\x^2&=e^2\\text{ or }e^4\\\\x&=\\pm e\\text{ or }\\pm e^2\\end{align*}$$\n\nAll four values are nonzero and satisfy the original equation.",
